# FreeCAD-9rc independent analytical oracles

These are software qualification benchmarks for the new coupled contact
domain. They are not an Oomakhi model, a contact-law recommendation, or building
design acceptance. The signed references and numerical budgets below are
derived before a successful native candidate run. Only the root agent runs
FreeCAD, OCC, CalculiX, GUI tests or builds. The existing FreeCAD-960 and
FreeCAD-sv7 domains remain independently qualified and unchanged.

The first installed-app refusal is a baseline, not numerical qualification.
This document does not infer contact sample count or identity from a mesh face.
Ordinary beam FRD `S` values remain section forces/moments, never MPa.

## Stable, physically connected normal-contact specimen

The reference geometry is a straight chain, ordered from the physical support
to the applied beam load:

`Fixed anchored prism -> genuine Tet contact -> guided loaded prism -> detached
solid RBE reference -> scalar SPRING2 -> original beam vertex -> beam tip`.

The two solids are real CAD triangular prisms, not receiving-node padding.
Their common undeformed interface consists of geometrically coincident faces
with distinct node identities and distinct solid owners. No beam node belongs
to the RBE, a contact face, or a Tie surface.

