Public RigidBody examples spell its constrained mode `Constraint`; descriptive
wording such as “fixed guide” is not an instruction to invent a `Fixed` enum
value. The guide is a declared physical support. Observe its actual native
forces and couples separately from the internal RBE transfer and from native
algebraic equation terms, even when statics predicts every guide action zero.

The new guide is necessary. A fully free loaded-solid RBE, scalar X spring and
frictionless planar contact leave two tangential translations and rotation
about X unrestrained. Opening also removes normal contact stiffness. Neither a
singular solve nor artificial weak stabilization is a qualification control.
This is a new bounded support domain, not a claim that old sv7's fully free RBE
automatically supplies those missing physical constraints.

Beam, solid and volume-owned boundary-face element IDs must be globally
disjoint. The actual authored candidate uses beam elements `1..2`, loaded-solid
elements `101..103`, backing-solid elements `301..303`, backing original nodes
`301..306`, and boundary faces `501+`. These avoid the collision that would arise by
reusing sv7's old boundary face IDs `201..208`. Bind these real structural IDs
to the actual stock export; detached reference and spring labels remain
writer-allocated and must not be guessed.

After the native export's documented first-two-node Tet4 permutation, each
prism's three tetrahedra have determinant `3000 mm³` and volume `500 mm³`.
Their sum is the real `1500 mm³` prism volume. A standard-library rational
arithmetic check of the authored coordinates gives these values exactly;
the actual emitted deck still has to retain that positive orientation.

The public stock interface assigns every Contact reference except the last to
the slave side and the last reference to the master side
([meshsetsgetter.py](/Users/zukomgwili/src/FreeCAD/src/Mod/Fem/femmesh/meshsetsgetter.py:525)).
The installed-refusal candidate's order `[backing face, loaded face]` therefore
means backing **slave**, loaded prism **master**. The physical free-body values
below do not depend on swapping those roles, but sample/element/face ownership
and normal direction do. Bind the actual stock-exported side order explicitly;
never rename it from the physical loading direction or a sorted owner list.

## Independent signed forces and original-global origin moments

All forces below act **on the named owner** and use original global XYZ axes.
Moments are about the global origin. The loading line passes through both
triangle centroids and the beam centroid, so no physical local couple is
applied. Translating the specimen off the global axes makes force transport
observable.

| Action | Force `(Fx,Fy,Fz)` N | Origin moment `(Mx,My,Mz)` N mm |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Source on beam tip | `(-100,0,0)` | `(0,2300,1700)` |
| Spring on beam root | `(100,0,0)` | `(0,-2300,-1700)` |
| Spring on RBE reference | `(-100,0,0)` | `(0,2300,1700)` |
| RBE on detached reference | `(100,0,0)` | `(0,-2300,-1700)` |
| RBE on loaded-solid receiving nodes | `(-100,0,0)` | `(0,2300,1700)` |
| Contact on loaded solid | `(100,0,0)` | `(0,-2300,-1700)` |
| Contact on anchored solid | `(-100,0,0)` | `(0,2300,1700)` |
| Physical Fixed support on anchored solid | `(100,0,0)` | `(0,-2300,-1700)` |
| Beam physical guide | `(0,0,0)` | `(0,0,0)` |
| Loaded-solid physical guide | `(0,0,0)` | `(0,0,0)` |

Check five independently selected free bodies: beam (source/spring/guide),
detached reference (spring/RBE/guide), loaded solid (RBE/contact), anchored
solid (contact/Fixed), and whole model (source/physical supports). The paired
spring, RBE and contact actions must cancel internally; none is an additional
external ground support. Native rotation-reference actions are physical
couples. An algebraic dummy coordinate is not a physical force arm.

Every beam element has outward first-end force `(100,0,0) N` and last-end force
`(-100,0,0) N`, zero centroid-relative moments and compressive axial channel
`-100 N`. Both shear channels, both bending channels and torque are zero.
Project on the actual reported native face axes; do not assume the first-end
basis is right handed. Keep all six signed components and explicit element,
original node, end, material, section, owner, units and same-case frame identity.

## Conditional affine patch and penalty-compliance references

The source is statically determinate: each prism carries `P=100 N` in
compression. At `nu=0`, uniform axial strain with zero other displacement
components satisfies free lateral faces, the anchored prism far clamp, rigid loaded
near-face motion and the symmetric planar contact patch. Each C3D4 represents
that affine field exactly. Therefore every genuine solid stress row has:

```
Sxx = -P/A = -4/3 MPa
Syy = Szz = Sxy = Sxz = Syz = 0 MPa
```

For face-to-face LINEAR contact only, the official manual establishes a linear
pressure/overclosure relation through the origin using only the slope. It does
not use the node-to-face regularization parameters. The references, independently
read after the installed baseline, are CalculiX 2.23 manual
§6.7.7 p244 and §7.130 pp615–616
([official manual](https://www.dhondt.de/ccx_2.23.pdf)). These normal-law and
sign assumptions must be checked against the actual stock written law and
native output before using the following displacement values as acceptance
references; they do not apply to regularized node-to-face LINEAR contact.

```
pressure                         = P/A = 1.3333333333333333 MPa
contact clearance                = -P/(A*K_n) = -0.000013333333333333333 mm
compression of either prism      = P*20/(E*A) = 0.00013333333333333333 mm
anchored interface Ux              = -0.00013333333333333333 mm
loaded interface Ux               = -0.00014666666666666667 mm
loaded RBE reference Ux          = -0.00028 mm
beam root minus RBE reference Ux = -P/k = -0.01 mm
beam root Ux                     = -0.01028 mm
```

The exact rational references are `p=4/3`, clearance `-1/75000`, anchored
interface `-1/7500`, loaded interface `-11/75000`, RBE reference `-7/25000`
and beam root `-257/25000`, in the respective MPa/mm units above.

Contact pressure is positive, while compressive solid `Sxx` is negative.
Native sample normals and tangents are authoritative. A face-to-face contact
sample is an actual overlap integration point: three interface corner nodes
do not imply three samples. Preserve native pair/owner/element/face/sample and
master projection identities within their documented frame-local scope.

The elementary uniform-traction beam extension `PL/(EA_beam)` is not an exact
native B32R endpoint-displacement reference: stock vertex point loading uses
expanded corner-mean work-conjugate loading. That sv7 limitation remains
unqualified. If beam-displacement equivalence is checked, use a separate public
native beam with the same mesh, section, material and negative source, but root
motion independently prescribed to `-0.01028 mm`; do not fit its root or tip to
the coupled result. A match qualifies composition equivalence, not continuum
beam end compliance.

## Frozen compression numerical budgets

These are fixture-specific absolute requirements, not Oomakhi's 1%/5% project
limits and not a universal solver guarantee. Full-precision native observer
values should dominate comparison; ordinary FRD displacement/stress printing
may use only six or seven significant digits.

| Check | Absolute budget | Independent scale |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Each physical/internal action force and free-body force closure | `0.01 N` | `10^-4` of the declared 100-N source |
| Original-global action-moment and free-body moment closure | `1 N mm` | Force budget transported through a 100-mm characteristic length |
| Each beam-end force/local force channel | `0.1 N` | `10^-3` constant-force patch budget, preserving sv7's separate native section-integration allowance |
| Each beam-end centroid-relative moment/local moment channel | `0.4 N mm` | `10^-3 * P * 4-mm` section depth, including expected-zero channels |
| Every genuine solid stress component | `0.0001 MPa` | Affine C3D4 stress patch and printed-value budget |
| Every active local normal pressure | `0.001 MPa` | `0.075%` of independent `P/A`; no averaging of duplicate identities |
| Native normal-law clearance | `0.00000001 mm` | The same pressure budget divided by `K_n` |
| Contact representative area sum, if exposed | `0.001 mm²` | `1.34e-5` of the exact 75-mm² planar overlap |
| Anchored/loaded interface and RBE-reference displacement | `0.0000001 mm` | More than ten times the ordinary printed displacement rounding bound |
| Spring relative displacement and beam-root displacement | `0.000001 mm` | `10^-4` of the exact spring compression |
| Independently prescribed pure/coupled beam displacement equivalence | `0.0000002 mm` | Same native discretization and conservative printed-value addition budget |

Expected-zero tangential pressure/state channels must not be inferred from a
global normal-force agreement. In frictionless contact, preserve the actual
`FRICTIONLESS` state and unavailable tangential history. With friction enabled
and no tangent demand, require actual native `STICK` and zero plastic increment.
Do not infer stick merely because a printed tangential displacement is small.

## Stable prescribed-opening companion

Keep geometry, material, mesh, contact, connector, physical anchored-solid support and
both five-DOF guides. Replace the beam-tip Force by one actual X-displacement
source `+0.002 mm`; other tip DOFs remain free. There is no zero Force
placeholder and no nonzero dead load applied to an unsupported open body.

The tip displacement anchors the previously free axial rigid motion. At the
completed state, beam and loaded prism translate `+0.002 mm` in X without
strain; the spring has zero extension and the anchored prism remains at rest.
All beam, spring, RBE, source-reaction, guide, contact and Fixed-support forces
and moments are zero. All solid stress components are zero. At every retained
native preserved interface projection, measured clearance is `+0.002 mm`.
Pressure, shear and plastic/total tangential quantities are unavailable for
inactive native contact, not invented measured zeros. Use `UNAVAILABLE` with
the actual native open-projection availability/engagement labels.

Freeze opening displacement/clearance budget `1e-8 mm`, solid stress budget
`1e-5 MPa`, physical/internal force budget `0.001 N` and moment budget
`0.1 N mm`. These are absolute near-zero requirements chosen before observing
the open solve. A missing projection is not evidence of measured opening;
absence, native inactive projection and malformed/truncated output remain
distinct outcomes.

## Tangential-state companions are a distinct loading domain

The scalar X spring and its beam do not deliver a Y/Z shear source to the solid.
To test nonzero elastic sticking or irreversible sliding, author a real
tangential actuator, for example prescribed Y motion of the loaded RBE guide,
and report its external reaction separately from the internal port transfer.
Never hide it as a zero support or infer friction demand from a global force
that is absent from that load path.

An initial tiny prescribed Y motion (candidate `1e-6 mm`) can target elastic
stick; a larger motion (candidate `0.005 mm`) can target slip with `mu=0.3`.
These are proposals, not executed or qualified fixtures. Free-sided three-
dimensional prisms under tangent loading do not have a generally exact uniform
simple-shear stress/displacement field, so `q=G*Delta/(L1+L2)` is not a valid
unqualified oracle. For confirmed full same-direction sliding, Coulomb gives
the integrated bound `|T|=mu*P=30 N`; this equality requires actual local slip
direction/state and positive normal contact at the same completed frame, not
an assumption that all samples slide. Partial slip or stick instead requires
state-appropriate inequalities and independent owner/free-body closure. The
root agent must freeze any adopted tangential fixture and its bounds before
running it; no tangent response is accepted from this proposal alone.

## Ownership, refusal and history controls

The admitted contact surfaces must consist solely of genuine Tet boundary
faces from the two declared solid owners. Original beam, spring, RBE reference,
rotation and algebraic helper IDs cannot masquerade as contact material nodes.
Repeated pair/sample labels cannot be collapsed, assigned by coordinate order
or treated as persistent material points between frames. Same-time output is
insufficient to join cases without step/increment/case and owned-run custody.

Meaningful negative controls include a direct beam contact face; a beam node
added to the RBE's genuine receiving face; contact faces that cross owners or
overlap a physical support; duplicate/shared contact slave declarations; a
missing physical guide causing an inadmissible mechanism; opening with a
nonzero dead load and no axial anchor; mixed beam-resultant `S` interpreted as
solid MPa; mismatched or incomplete beam/contact frame identities; altered
input, output or native executable; and failed/cancelled/superseded reruns.
Refusals must withdraw Current data without erasing saved literal history.

Saving and opening in a separate process must preserve the exact beam and
contact data strings, their hashes, case/owner/sample identities, solver
requests, connector and support settings, solid-only stress ownership and
source maps. Restored results are Historical and not CompletedRun. An explicit
Current query may change the status to the documented historical/withdrawn
Stale reason; it must not promote history, repair source paths, run the solver,
or rewrite the saved observation. Both results must refer to the same original
case; no late rebinding of an old contact record to a newer beam run is allowed.

No failed response criterion may be weakened using observed numerical error.
An invalid oracle, authoring mistake or unsupported subdomain is retained
explicitly and distinguished from the successful qualification record.
